      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "provide a formal definition next.",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        230.734375,
        446.1108703613281,
        239.64093017578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Definition 3 (Backward Reachable Tube). For a set S, and",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        248.82997131347656,
        558.0009765625,
        257.89593505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "constant T > 0, the T-Backward Reachable Tube (T-BRT)",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        260.7850036621094,
        557.990966796875,
        269.63177490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is defined as:",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        272.98907470703125,
        367.76507568359375,
        281.57684326171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RT (S) := {x | ∀u ∈U(0,T ], ∃t ∈(0, T], s.t. ϕ(t, x, u) ∈S}.",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        290.81524658203125,
        558.5930786132812,
        309.3321533203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When T",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        312.9680480957031,
        347.3616943359375,
        321.8148193359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "= ∞, we refer to it simply as the Backward",
      "bbox": [
        355.5310363769531,
        312.16107177734375,
        558.0009765625,
        329.4461669921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Reachable Tube (BRT) and denote by R(S).",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        324.1160583496094,
        496.0335388183594,
        341.4011535644531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To construct the BRT, the HJ reachability procedure casts",
      "bbox": [
        323.1629638671875,
        343.3374328613281,
        558.0012817382812,
        352.2439880371094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the safety verification task as an optimal control problem.",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        355.29241943359375,
        558.0009155273438,
        364.198974609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Here, the controller’s objective is to avoid the unsafe set",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        367.2474060058594,
        558.0008544921875,
        376.1539611816406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Xu. This is quantitatively expressed through a value function",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        378.2370300292969,
        558.0021362304688,
        395.5221252441406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "V (x, t) := mins∈[−t,0] l(ϕ(s, x, u)), which measures the",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        390.9989929199219,
        558.0175170898438,
        401.644775390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "minimum cost or the distance to entry Xu. In the absence",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        402.1470031738281,
        558.0003051757812,
        419.4320983886719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of disturbances, the evolution of V (x, t) is governed by a",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        414.9089660644531,
        558.0009765625,
        423.97491455078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hamilton-Jacobi-Isaacs Variational Inequality that takes the",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        427.0233459472656,
        558.0008544921875,
        435.9299011230469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "form of a Hamilton–Jacobi–Bellman equation [3]:",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        438.9793395996094,
        518.2401123046875,
        447.8858947753906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "min{DtV (x, t) + H(x, t, ∇V (x, t)), l(x) −V (x, t)} = 0,",
      "bbox": [
        317.3419494628906,
        458.1259765625,
        553.89013671875,
        475.41107177734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where l(x) is the terminal condition where V (x, 0) = l(x),",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        479.0469665527344,
        558.0108642578125,
        488.1129150390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and H(x, t, ∇V (x, t)) := maxu∈U DxV (x, t) · f(x, u).",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        490.1949768066406,
        538.8568725585938,
        507.4800720214844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Once V (x, T) is computed, the T-BRT is given by the",
      "bbox": [
        323.16290283203125,
        503.2799377441406,
        558.0013427734375,
        512.3458862304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sublevel set",
      "bbox": [
        313.19989013671875,
        515.394287109375,
        360.56207275390625,
        524.3008422851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RT (Xu) = {x | V (x, T) ≤0, x ∈Xu},",
      "bbox": [
        355.2138977050781,
        534.5409545898438,
        515.9878540039062,
        551.8260498046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "which implies that any state within this set will eventually",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        555.621337890625,
        558.0008544921875,
        564.5278930664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lead to Xu under any control u(·) within less than T units",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        566.6099243164062,
        558.0011596679688,
        583.89501953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of time. HJ reachability gives rigorous safety guarantees",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        579.5313110351562,
        558.0009155273438,
        588.4378662109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "when x ∈Rc",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        589.7861328125,
        377.6245422363281,
        607.8060302734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "+∞(Xu), which is the largest safe control",
      "bbox": [
        374.0609436035156,
        590.5209350585938,
        558.0018920898438,
        607.8060302734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "invariant set, but is computational costly in high dimensions.",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        603.4423217773438,
        558.0008544921875,
        612.348876953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Efficient solvers for the HJ PDE mitigate this [3], improving",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        615.3973388671875,
        558.0010375976562,
        624.3038940429688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "practicality. Our work tackles safety from a complementary",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        627.352294921875,
        558.0009155273438,
        636.2588500976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "angle.",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        639.3073120117188,
        337.26959228515625,
        648.2138671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "D. Control Barrier Functions",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        660.8189697265625,
        435.1321716308594,
        669.40673828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CBFs offer another conservative alternative to HJ reacha-",
      "bbox": [
        323.1629638671875,
        676.9512939453125,
        558.0013427734375,
        685.8578491210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "bility. By bounding ˙h with an extended class-K function, they",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        686.118896484375,
        557.9989624023438,
        705.22607421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "render a chosen set C control invariant and thus ensure safety.",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        699.8959350585938,
        558.0009155273438,
        717.1810302734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To formally introduce CBFs we are required to introduce the",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        712.8173217773438,
        558.0009765625,
        721.723876953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
